DECL	{"args":[{"name":"a","sort":{"sort":"track"}}],"body":{"rises":{"and":[{"and":[{"cmp":"ge","lhs":{"abs":{"args":[{"var":"a"}],"params":[{"param":"window"}],"quantity":"prim_heading_change"}},"rhs":{"param":"u_turn_min"}},{"cmp":"le","lhs":{"abs":{"args":[{"var":"a"}],"params":[{"param":"window"}],"quantity":"prim_heading_change"}},"rhs":{"sub":[{"lit":{"den":1,"num":360},"unit":"degree"},{"param":"u_turn_min"}]}}]},{"cmp":"le","lhs":{"abs":{"args":[{"var":"a"}],"measure":"kin_yaw_rate"}},"rhs":{"param":"yaw_tol"}}]}},"contract":"Road user a has turned \"so as to proceed in the opposite direction\": its heading has reversed, \"whether accomplished by one continuous movement or not\". The magnitude of its heading change over the window behind the observation (prim.heading_change over a window of length window, degrees, positive to the left) lies in the band from u_turn_min to 360 degrees minus u_turn_min, both inclusive, so that a turn short of a reversal and a full loop both lie outside it; a reversal to either hand is denoted, and one made in several movements, with halts or backing between them, is denoted where its integrated heading change lies in the band. The act begins within the window behind the observation at which it is recognized. The act is recognized at the observation at which the magnitude of the heading change over the window behind lies in that band and a's yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate) is at most yaw_tol in magnitude, where this did not hold at the previous observation: the heading has stopped turning. The concept holds at that observation only, and not again until that condition has ceased to hold and then holds again. Conduct before the window behind is not read: a reversal that takes longer than the window is not recognized. It denotes the change of a's heading only: it says nothing of the way on which a turns, of its class, of its speed, or of why it turns. Not denoted: a heading change smaller than u_turn_min, such as a turn to the left or the right; a full loop, whose heading change exceeds 360 degrees minus u_turn_min; a reversal still under way, whose yaw rate exceeds yaw_tol. Where the window is truncated or a yaw rate in it is missing, it is unknown.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484B-077","id":"drv.motion.u_turn","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[{"name":"window","unit":"second"},{"name":"u_turn_min","unit":"degree"},{"name":"yaw_tol","unit":"degree_per_second"}],"residues":["The class of the road user and the place of the turn are the caller's: the concept denotes the reversal of heading for any road user anywhere, and a law reads the class and the place beside it."],"supersedes":null}
